✅ Features Used in NOVA AI Project
🧠 AI & Natural Language Understanding
Accepts user input via GUI (text-based interaction).

Parses user commands from natural language.

Responds with either:

Direct text replies (via command lookup)

System commands based on matched keywords

Uses a commands.json file to map text input to system commands.

🖥️ Graphical User Interface (GUI)
Built using Tkinter (Python standard GUI library)

Features:

Text input field

Chat history display (for conversations)

Camera toggle button (in-progress feature)

Return key binding to trigger assistant logic

⚙️ System Command Execution
Runs basic Windows system apps like:

Calculator (calc)

Notepad (notepad)

Microsoft Office apps (via full file paths, attempted)

Uses os.system() or subprocess to execute .exe files via paths defined in commands.json

📁 Custom JSON-Based Command Management
External file: commands.json

Maps text like "open excel" to real executable paths (e.g., C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft Office\\root\\Office16\\EXCEL.EXE)

Easily editable to add/remove/update commands

🔐 API Integration Setup (Attempted)
Configured config.json for API key storage

Attempted to integrate:

Gemini AI API (by Google)

(Possibly OpenAI/GPT in the future)

Basic structure for calling APIs with authentication

